# OpenFoundry — Code owners
#
# This file routes pull-request reviews to the team(s) responsible for each
# area of the monorepo. The last matching pattern wins, so put more specific
# rules below the generic ones.
#
# Routes to the verified repository owner until real team assignments exist.
# Every entry is rewritten, not only the catch-all: GitHub assigns no code
# owner for a nonexistent team, and the last matching pattern wins without
# falling back, so leftover @open-foundry/* entries would silently unroute
# their paths. CODEOWNERS is routing only: required approval must also be
# configured in repository rules. Authors cannot supply their own required
# approval. Replace entries with actual collaborators as responsibility is
# delegated.
#
# Reference: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-security/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

